<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended higher on Thursday, but well off peaks, in a day dominated by worries about Europe's single currency project.</p>
<p>The market lacked fresh domestic impact and remained tied to currency moves, and to sister markets in Germany and Italy.</p>
<p>Stability in the peseta and the lira helped bonds keep their footing, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The fact that the peseta has been stable at levels of about 84.60 is, without doubt, a tranquilising factor for bonds,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
</text>
